cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Conformal quantile convention probes: harnesses for auditing finite-sample validity in conformal-prediction implementations"
message: "If you use these probes or their measurements, please cite this artifact."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lalakiya
    given-names: Shivam
    # TODO: add orcid if you have one, e.g. orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # TODO: decide affiliation. Leaving it out avoids implying institutional endorsement
    #       of an independent research artifact. Add only if you want it attached.
license: MIT
# TODO: confirm the owner — change if the repo lives under an org rather than your personal account
repository-code: "https://github.com/shivamlalakiya/conformal-coverage-audit"
abstract: >-
  Measurement harnesses used to audit how Python conformal-prediction
  implementations resolve the conformal quantile at finite sample sizes. Each
  script validates its closed forms against exact rational arithmetic at import
  time, and each writes a plain-text output file that is committed alongside it.
  Covers the convention in isolation, sktime, river, darts, statsforecast, and a
  rebuttal probe that adjudicates a retracted finding of the authors' own.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - finite-sample coverage
  - order statistics
  - prediction intervals
  - software correctness
  - reproducibility
